00:03:17.430 --> 00:03:18.198
Why are you saying that?

00:03:18.198 --> 00:03:20.433
Well, it's I mean, clearly,

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.334
there are some that

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.069
that are getting bailed out. Right.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.371
You know, the depositors of these these

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.907
these particular banks are

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.543
many of which are companies. Right.

00:03:30.543 --> 00:03:31.978
They need to make payroll.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.879
The money was trapped

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.380
in these institutions.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:35.949
And so the government

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.350
took extraordinary actions

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.786
to allow them to access that money.

00:03:39.919 --> 00:03:40.153
Right.

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:41.521
Even even as those banks

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.856
were going through receivership and

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.024
and had failed.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:47.994
So whether the taxpayer money

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.396
was used to to

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.764
to implement those plans,

00:03:51.764 --> 00:03:53.466
the government said no.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:56.402
But but clearly, there was a rescue

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.570
of a particular group

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.572
of people and businesses.

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:02.375
So one of the things that M.J.

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:02.642
noted

00:04:02.642 --> 00:04:03.309
that's really important

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:03.977
is what

00:04:03.977 --> 00:04:04.944
the government's doing now

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.779
and they're setting up this emergency

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.248
lending facility.

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.249
So part of the reason

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.317
the city got into a lot of trouble

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:12.619
is that they had to sell these long

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:14.087
term treasuries at a loss.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:15.388
Then they went out to try to capital

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.689
raise last Wednesday,

00:04:16.689 --> 00:04:17.857
spooked the policy

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.859
to try to get $2 billion.

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:21.527
And they saw and depositors

00:04:21.527 --> 00:04:24.063
well, and investors saw the loss

00:04:24.497 --> 00:04:25.531
and pulled out money.

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:27.300
And so you're selling these at a loss

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.601
because interest rates have gone up.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.003
Your securities aren't as

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:31.404
attractive anymore.

00:04:31.404 --> 00:04:32.972
This what the government's doing

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.440
now would prevent against someone else

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.209
having to do a capital raise like that.

00:04:36.209 --> 00:04:36.776
Right? Right.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:37.810
That's exactly it.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.612
Banking is all about confidence, right?

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.580
Confidence in the system.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.382
Confidence that if you or I

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.182
or anyone here at this

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:44.784
table puts their money into a bank,

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.052
if we need it tomorrow,

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:47.220
that money will be there.

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:47.920
What happened here

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:49.889
with SVB was a lack of confidence.

00:04:49.889 --> 00:04:50.857
And so you started to see

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.525
all of these depositors rush

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.093
to get all of their money out.

00:04:54.093 --> 00:04:56.129
And that's what led to this panic.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.196
So what the Fed is trying to do

00:04:57.196 --> 00:04:59.132
and what regulators are trying to do here

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:01.634
is to prevent that from happening again.

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:01.901
Right.

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:02.669
Sort of

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:04.003
insulate the riskier

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:05.371
insulate the contagion

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:06.572
so that this doesn't spread

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:08.708
beyond and sob story.

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:10.109
And that's why you saw officials

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.811
in layman's terms, this an old fashioned

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:12.679
is it an old fashioned

00:05:12.679 --> 00:05:13.846
run on the bank as well?

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.581
Absolutely. 100%.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.349
And I mean, you know,

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:17.183
I spoke to a founder

00:05:17.183 --> 00:05:18.651
